 - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.
 
 Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).
+
+## Store finder
+
+- Admin sign-in uses the username `admin` and the password from `ADMIN_PASSWORD` (read at startup; unset/empty disables admin sign-in), e.g. `docker run -p 8000:8000 -e ADMIN_PASSWORD=... -v $PWD/data:/app/data <image>`.
+- The SQLite database is `data/app.db`; 8 sample stores are seeded on first start only.
+- Backend tests: `pip install pytest && pytest backend/tests`. Frontend type check: `npm run typecheck` in `frontend/`.
